<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hoffmann-La Roche</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1896</span> · Also known as Roche</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hoffmann-La Roche, usually known as Roche, is a Swiss pharmaceutical and diagnostics company founded in Basel in 1896 by Fritz Hoffmann-La Roche. It grew out of the Basel chemical tradition into one of the largest pharmaceutical firms in the world, known for products such as Valium and, later, cancer medicines and diagnostic tests.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hoffmann-la-roche.jpg" alt="Hoffmann-La Roche" width="320" height="167" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: F. Hoffmann-La Roche AG / Pentagram · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:F._Hoffmann-La_Roche_2021_logo.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
